    "Types 0,1,2,4,5,6,8,9,10 and defined type15 exact/clamp fallback; key pointer alignments 0,1,2,3; optimized layouts require even pointers.",
    "Exact/interior/clamp/wrapped frames; flags 0..15; history at zero, last key, out of range and 65535; unequal axis counts; valid one-key exact/nonwrapping clamps.",
    "Persistent histories through forward, reverse, looping, ignored history and clip bytes replaced at the same address; constant tracks and signed zero.",
    "Defined later-axis search exhaustion after an earlier axis initializes stale val/tan; whole-call fallback preserves histories, output words, return and log trace.",
    "Defined clamped float payloads preserve negative zero, infinity and a quiet-NaN payload as 32-bit words; no NaN interpolation claim.",
